// Immediate transitions out of both regions' initial states: the first region's is merged into the GO block (it
// comes right after the root's code), the second region's comes after the first region's other guards and counts a
// taken transition as the first did, so it stays in an if (_GO) of its own and i = 5 runs after the inputs are
// read.
scchart Main {
  input int i
  input bool c
  output int o, y
  region { initial state A immediate do y = 2 go to A1 state A1 if c go to A2 state A2 }
  region { initial state P immediate do i = 5; o = i go to Q state Q if c go to R state R }
}
